{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":484746,"name":"Aviv Yeshayav","username":"TheAviv","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/theaviv/{size}/119258_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-06T23:43:35.235Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484746-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484746-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484746-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484746-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eProduct: Grok Bot / Gmail MCP\u003cbr\u003e\nAccount: aviv@theaviv.ca\u003cbr\u003e\nNamespace: user-Gmail–professional-aviv-theaviv-ca\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot’s Gmail connector cannot search Spam even though the label metadata reports Spam threads.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484746-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484746-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCall list_labels — SPAM showed threadsTotal=3, threadsUnread=3.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCall search_threads with query in:spam.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAlso try label:SPAM, is:spam, and broader queries with includeTrash.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCompare with an Inbox search.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484746-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484746-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003esearch_threads returns the Spam threads so an agent can review Spam without using the browser.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484746-operating-system-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484746-operating-system-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOther\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484746-version-information-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484746-version-information-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eN/A — Gmail MCP connector issue; no Grok Bot version information available.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484746-additional-information-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484746-additional-information-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAdditional Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eActual: search_threads returns empty {} every time. Inbox search works, while list_labels still shows the Spam count.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eImpact: cannot review or empty Spam via the connector for a query form the tool docs claim (in:spam / label:SPAM). Forced browser fallback.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAlso filed via in-app Send Feedback and by email to \u003ca href=\"mailto:hi@cursor.com\"\u003ehi@cursor.com\u003c/a\u003e from aviv@theaviv.ca (thread subject: Grok Bot Gmail: search_threads returns empty for Spam while list_labels shows 3 threads).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484746-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484746-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo - Cursor works, but with this issue\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-06T23:43:43.400Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":8,"reads":5,"readers_count":4,"score":41.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":170832,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-gmail-search-threads-returns-empty-for-spam-while-list-labels-shows-threads","display_username":"Aviv Yeshayav","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":135276,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-gmail-search-threads-returns-empty-for-spam-while-list-labels-shows-threads/170832/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":484834,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-07T04:20:01.315Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, thanks for the detailed report.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Gmail connector works on top of Google’s hosted Gmail server, and its search excludes Spam and Trash by default. The \u003ccode\u003eincludeTrash\u003c/code\u003e option only adds Trash, and \u003ccode\u003ein:spam\u003c/code\u003e / \u003ccode\u003elabel:SPAM\u003c/code\u003e / \u003ccode\u003eis:spam\u003c/code\u003e don’t override that default. That’s why you get an empty result even though \u003ccode\u003elist_labels\u003c/code\u003e still shows a count.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe documented way to reach Spam is the \u003ccode\u003ein:anywhere\u003c/code\u003e operator. Can you try it and tell me what you get back?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAsk the bot to call \u003ccode\u003esearch_threads\u003c/code\u003e with this exact request: \u003ccode\u003ein:anywhere label:SPAM\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIf it’s empty, try \u003ccode\u003esearch_threads\u003c/code\u003e with: \u003ccode\u003ein:anywhere is:unread\u003c/code\u003e your 3 Spam threads are unread, so they should show up with the SPAM label id\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eReply here with whether step 1 or step 2 returned threads, or if it’s still empty.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOne expectation note: the connector can move threads to Trash or Spam and change labels, but Google’s server doesn’t expose a permanent delete tool. So you can’t “clear” Spam through the connector right now, even once the threads are found.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLet me know what \u003ccode\u003ein:anywhere\u003c/code\u003e shows, since the next steps depend on that.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-07T04:20:01.315Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":4,"readers_count":3,"score":0.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":170832,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-gmail-search-threads-returns-empty-for-spam-while-list-labels-shows-threads","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-gmail-search-threads-returns-empty-for-spam-while-list-labels-shows-threads/170832/5","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":485807,"name":"Aviv Yeshayav","username":"TheAviv","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/theaviv/{size}/119258_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-07T22:28:05.643Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eTried both as asked on aviv@theaviv.ca just now.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003esearch_threads query \u003ccode\u003ein:anywhere label:SPAM\u003c/code\u003e → empty {}.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003esearch_threads query \u003ccode\u003ein:anywhere is:spam\u003c/code\u003e (and with includeTrash) → empty {}.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003esearch_threads query \u003ccode\u003ein:anywhere is:unread\u003c/code\u003e → returns unread threads (inbox), works.\u003cbr\u003e\nCaveat: list_labels SPAM is threadsTotal=0 / threadsUnread=0 right now, so an empty Spam search is expected today and doesn’t re-prove the original gap. When I filed, list_labels showed threadsTotal=3 / threadsUnread=3 and every spam query including in:spam / label:SPAM returned empty while inbox search worked. That mismatch is still the bug (email T-F54576). Happy to re-run the in:anywhere tests the next time Spam has mail again.\u003cbr\u003e\nNoted on permanent delete: understood.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-07T22:32:35.753Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":5.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":170832,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-gmail-search-threads-returns-empty-for-spam-while-list-labels-shows-threads","display_username":"Aviv Yeshayav","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":135276,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-gmail-search-threads-returns-empty-for-spam-while-list-labels-shows-threads/170832/6","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":486742,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-08T18:12:03.176Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThanks for testing both options and catching the nuance. You got it right.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSince \u003ccode\u003elist_labels\u003c/code\u003e currently shows SPAM with \u003ccode\u003ethreadsTotal=0 / threadsUnread=0\u003c/code\u003e, an empty response for a Spam request is expected and doesn’t really confirm the original issue. The fact that \u003ccode\u003ein:anywhere is:unread\u003c/code\u003e returned threads also confirms the connector itself is working fine.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo fully close this out, we need one conclusive run exactly when there are emails in Spam again. At that moment, please call \u003ccode\u003esearch_threads\u003c/code\u003e with this exact request:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ccode\u003ein:anywhere label:SPAM\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis operator is documented on the hosted Gmail server as the way to reach Spam and Trash, unlike \u003ccode\u003ein:spam\u003c/code\u003e / \u003ccode\u003elabel:SPAM\u003c/code\u003e / \u003ccode\u003eis:spam\u003c/code\u003e / \u003ccode\u003eincludeTrash\u003c/code\u003e, which don’t override the default behavior. Please reply here with whether it returns those threads or still returns \u003ccode\u003e{}\u003c/code\u003e. The next steps depend on that.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn permanent delete, yep, that’s correct. The connector can move items to Trash or Spam and change labels, but Google doesn’t expose a tool for permanent deletion, so we can’t clear Spam through the connector right now.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-08T18:12:03.176Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":6,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":0.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":170832,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-gmail-search-threads-returns-empty-for-spam-while-list-labels-shows-threads","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","reply_to_user":{"id":135276,"username":"TheAviv","name":"Aviv Yeshayav","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/theaviv/{size}/119258_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-gmail-search-threads-returns-empty-for-spam-while-list-labels-shows-threads/170832/7","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":486799,"name":"Aviv Yeshayav","username":"TheAviv","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/theaviv/{size}/119258_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-08T20:06:28.538Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eRetest just now on aviv@theaviv.ca (2026-09-08 ~4pm America/Toronto). Spam has mail again.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003elist_labels SPAM: threadsTotal=1, threadsUnread=1, messagesTotal=1.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003esearch_threads query \u003ccode\u003ein:anywhere label:SPAM\u003c/code\u003e → empty {}.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003col start=\"2\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003esearch_threads query \u003ccode\u003ein:anywhere in:spam\u003c/code\u003e → empty {}.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003col start=\"3\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003esearch_threads with includeTrash=true and query \u003ccode\u003ein:anywhere label:SPAM\u003c/code\u003e → empty {}.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003col start=\"4\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003esearch_threads query \u003ccode\u003ein:anywhere is:unread\u003c/code\u003e → returns normal unread inbox threads (works). The Spam thread is not among them.\u003cbr\u003e\nSo with Spam non-empty, Dean’s documented \u003ccode\u003ein:anywhere\u003c/code\u003e path still cannot list Spam. Same mismatch as the original report (email T-F54576). Browser Gmail still shows the Spam thread.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e","post_number":8,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-08T20:06:28.538Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":1,"readers_count":0,"score":0.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":170832,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-gmail-search-threads-returns-empty-for-spam-while-list-labels-shows-threads","display_username":"Aviv Yeshayav","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":135276,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-gm